      "content": "In scenarios where lead time is highly variable, you might want to utilize a higher safety stock to accommodate those fluctuations. To adjust for inconsistent lead times in your formula, you can calculate the safety stock for the maximum anticipated lead time and the average lead time, then take the higher of the two:\n\nSafety Stock = Max (Max Daily Usage * Max Lead Time / 2 - Average Daily Usage * Max Lead Time / 4, Average Daily Usage * Max Lead Time / 2 - Max Daily Usage * Max Lead Time / 4)\n\nBy considering both the maximum and average scenarios, you ensure a higher buffer against unexpected delays. Furthermore, regularly reviewing and updating your inventory levels based on the latest lead time data from your suppliers will help you maintain a more accurate safety stock level.",
